# Partial rates of the Chargino based on M. Ibe, Y. Nakayama and S. Shirai (2023), https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.08087
# The decay rate is normalized to the decay of a Higgsino-like chargino into a single neutralino. 
# To account for the complete decay process, it is necessary to sum the decay rates into the other neutralinos. 
# In the case of the Wino, the decay rate should be multiplied by 4.
# All the units are GeV.
# Columns:
# 1. Chargino Mass  2. Mass Difference between Chargino and Neutralino  3. Total Width  4. Electron 5. Muon 6. Single pion 7. Total non-strange multi-hadron 8. pi- pi0 9. pi- pi- pi+ 10. pi- pi0 pi0 11. single K 12. K pi 13. K (2+)pi

